course: dictionary
lesson: 4453
title: Hanukkah, a festival of lights
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A proper noun is the name of one particular person, place or thing, so it starts with a capital letter. Hanukkah is a proper noun: it is the name of one special Jewish festival. Diwali and Eid are proper nouns too.
explain: Context helps you understand it. «Hanukkah is a Jewish festival of lights that lasts eight nights, with a candle lit on the menorah each night.» The words festival of lights and lit tell you it is a celebration with lots of light, and the menorah is the candle holder used for it.
explain: The same festival can be spelled in more than one way: Hanukkah, Chanukah and Hanukah all name the same festival. When you meet a new spelling, check a dictionary, then try the word in a sentence to see if it fits.
fact: Hanukkah is a Jewish festival of lights.
fact: Hanukkah lasts eight days and nights, in the winter.
fact: The festival remembers how the Temple in Jerusalem was won back and made holy again.
fact: Families light one more candle each night on a menorah with nine branches, and play dreidel.
fact: Hanukkah falls on different dates each year because it follows a lunar calendar, which follows the Moon.
exercise: «Hanukkah is a Jewish festival of lights that lasts eight nights.» What is Hanukkah? | A type of candle that burns for one hour | A one-day summer picnic | *A Jewish festival of lights that lasts eight nights | A Jewish holy book
exercise: «Families light one more candle each night on the menorah.» What do families do each night? | Put out all the candles | Sleep in the Temple | Eat one latke and go to bed | *Light one more candle
exercise: Why do the dates of Hanukkah change each year? | Because it is always on the same day | Because it is a summer festival | Because the Temple moves to a new place | *Because it follows a calendar that follows the Moon
test: «The eight nights of Hanukkah» means how many nights does Hanukkah last? | *Eight | Nine | Five | Seven
test: Hanukkah remembers the Temple in Jerusalem being won back and made what? | Empty | Loud | Old | *Holy
exam: According to «When classmates celebrate Christmas, Diwali, Eid, Hanukkah or Lunar New Year, you are respectful of their traditions», what should you show? | *Respect for the way classmates celebrate | Silence about your own | Loud complaints | Mockery of their festivals
